  "text": "That sounds like a wonderful idea! A classic breakfast omelette is simple, comforting, and perfect for a special morning. Here's how to make it:\n\n### Classic Breakfast Omelette\n\n**Ingredients** (serves 1):\n- 2 large eggs\n- 1/4 cup milk or yogurt (for fluffiness)\n- 1 tablespoon butter or oil (for cooking)\n- Salt and pepper to taste\n- Optional: cheese, spinach, mushrooms, or cooked ham for filling\n\n**Instructions**:\n1. **Crack the eggs** into a bowl and whisk them until the yolks are fully incorporated.\n2. Add the milk or yogurt and whisk again to combine.\n3. Heat a non-stick skillet over medium heat and add the butter or oil.\n4. Once the butter is melted, pour in the egg mixture.\n5. Let it cook for about 1-2 minutes, until the edges start to set.\n6. Use a spatula to gently push the edges toward the center, allowing the uncooked egg to flow to the edges.\n7. Once the omelette is mostly set, carefully flip it with a spatula.\n8. Cook for another 1-2 minutes, or until the top is fully cooked and golden.\n9. If using fillings, add them to one half of the omelette and fold the other half over.\n10. Serve immediately, optionally with toast, fruit, or syrup.\n\n### Tips:\n- For extra flavor, add fresh herbs like chives or dill.\n- Use a quality cheese like cheddar, Gouda, or Swiss for a cheesy twist.\n- If you want a lighter omelette, use egg whites only or reduce the milk/yogurt.\n\nYour mom will surely appreciate the effort and love in this breakfast \u2014 even if it\u2019s just one person\u2019s morning! \ud83c\udf73\u2764\ufe0f\n\nLet me know if you'd like a version with chocolate or other ingredients!",
